(>> 6.6 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: Detail the internal mechanics of the JavaScript Event Loop, explaining the) Tj
T*
(operational priority between the Microtask Queue and the Macrotask \(Callback\) Queue.) Tj
T*
(Answer: The JavaScript runtime contains a single Call Stack, Web APIs, a Callback) Tj
T*
(\(Macrotask\) Queue, and a Microtask Queue. When asynchronous APIs \(e.g. setTimeout\)) Tj
T*
(complete, their callbacks enter the Macrotask Queue. When Promises resolve \(.then,) Tj
T*
(.catch, await\), their callbacks enter the Microtask Queue. The Event Loop continuously) Tj
T*
(monitors the Call Stack. When the Call Stack empties, the Event Loop prioritizes the) Tj
T*
(Microtask Queue, draining EVERY microtask until the queue is completely empty. Only) Tj
T*
(after all microtasks are exhausted does the Event Loop take ONE macrotask from the) Tj
T*
(Macrotask Queue and push it onto the Call Stack. This explains why resolved Promise) Tj
T*
(callbacks execute before setTimeout\(..., 0\) callbacks.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Explain why 'fetch\(\)' does not reject on HTTP 404 or 500 status codes, and) Tj
T*
(demonstrate how robust client applications verify response success.) Tj
T*
(Answer: In the Fetch API, a Promise rejects strictly when a network-level failure occurs) Tj
T*
(that prevents the browser from completing the HTTP transaction \(e.g. loss of internet) Tj
T*
(connection, DNS resolution failure, CORS configuration rejection\). When a server) Tj
T*
(receives the request and returns an HTTP status code \(even an error code like 404 Not) Tj
T*
(Found or 500 Internal Server Error\), the HTTP communication succeeded. Consequently, the) Tj
T*
(fetch\(\) Promise fulfills successfully, returning a Response object. Robust applications) Tj
T*
(must check the boolean property 'response.ok' \(which is true only for status codes) Tj
T*
(200-299\) or inspect 'response.status'; if response.ok is false, the application must) Tj
T*
(throw a manual error to route into the catch block.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 6.7 Key Takeaways and Revision Points) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* The Event Loop drains the Microtask Queue \(Promises\) before the Macrotask Queue) Tj
T*
(\(setTimeout\).) Tj
T*
(* Async/await provides clean sequential syntax over Promise chains.) Tj
T*
(* Fetch API requires checking response.ok; it resolves normally on 404/500 HTTP) Tj
T*
